---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Epigraph from '../../components/Epigraph.astro';
import { identity } from '../../config/site';

/**
 * The Bengali section. The couplet and two words, and that is the whole page.
 *
 * This is NOT a Bengali edition of /blog/. Nothing here will be a rebuild
 * write-up in translation; the writing will be in Bengali and what it is about
 * is not decided yet. Anything on this page implying a parallel to the blog is
 * wrong — an earlier draft said "everything on the site so far is in English"
 * and linked across to it, and both were removed for saying exactly that.
 *
 * The band under the masthead used to sit on /blog/, over a list of English
 * essays. It belongs here: "বিশ্বমানব হবি যদি / শাশ্বত বাঙ্গালী হ’॥" is the
 * argument for the section existing, so it heads the section.
 *
 * WHAT IS NOT ON THIS PAGE, all of it built and then cut:
 *
 *   A heading. It read বাংলা, and the couplet above it is already two lines of
 *   Bengali — a page that opens in the script does not then need to be
 *   labelled with the name of the script. Romanising it to "Bangla" would have
 *   been worse, and for the same reason the romanised "GURUSADAY DUTT" was cut
 *   from under the verse.
 *
 *   A sentence saying the writing will be in Bengali. The couplet says it, and
 *   saying it again in English says it to the wrong reader.
 *
 *   A link out. The usual empty-state advice is never to leave a dead end, and
 *   that advice is written for an app screen with no navigation on it. This
 *   page has the site's own bar across the top, which is the way onward; a
 *   second copy of it in the body would be furniture.
 *
 * THE NOTICE IS SADHU BHASHA — শীঘ্রই আসিতেছে, not the everyday শীঘ্রই আসছে.
 * That is the register the couplet is already in: Gurusaday Dutt's verse is
 * 1930s, keeps his own older orthography in বাঙ্গালী, and closes on the sadhu
 * imperative হ’. A modern চলিত line under it would be two periods of the
 * language stacked in one column, which is the same mismatch the Bengali face
 * exists to prevent — the site sets Tiro Bangla precisely so the verse is not
 * left to whatever the reader's OS supplies. Chosen by the site's owner, who
 * is the native speaker; do not "modernise" it.
 *
 * No date, no countdown, no notify-me field — that would want a third-party
 * endpoint, which is the same reason the site has no contact form. Anyone who
 * wants telling has the blog's RSS.
 *
 * The <h1> is the page's label rather than its content, so it is `.sr-only`.
 * A screen reader gets "বাংলা", matching the <title> and the tab that led
 * here; the eye gets the couplet and the notice. `check:build` requires
 * exactly one <h1> per page, and a heading printed over a two-word page would
 * be louder than the page.
 *
 * **No `noindex`.** A placeholder is thin content when it is a bare
 * announcement; this one has the couplet, a real title and a real description.
 * The standard way this goes wrong is adding `noindex` "just for now" and
 * leaving it in on the day the section fills up.
 *
 * The description is in English on purpose. It is never painted on the page —
 * it is what a search result and a shared link show, and those are read by
 * people who have not arrived yet.
 */
---

<Base
  title="বাংলা"
  description={`The Bengali section of ${identity.name}'s site. Nothing published here yet.`}
  preloadBengali
>
  {
    /* Outside the block below on purpose: the band runs the full width of the
      viewport and belongs to the masthead above it. See Epigraph.astro. */
  }
  <Epigraph />

  <div class="shell bn">
    <h1 class="sr-only" lang="bn">বাংলা</h1>
    <p class="bn__soon" lang="bn">শীঘ্রই আসিতেছে</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The air is the composition. Two words inside a field this size read as a
     page waiting on purpose; the same words tucked under the band read as a
     page that failed to load the rest of itself. */
  .bn {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 2rem + 10vw, 10rem);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  /* Two Bengali rules, both of which the defaults get wrong:

       letter-spacing — must stay `normal`. The matra is one continuous
                        headstroke across the word and tracking cuts it into
                        pieces. Nothing here sets it, but nothing here may.
       font-weight    — Tiro Bangla loads at 400 only, and
                        `font-synthesis-weight: none` is global, so asking for
                        anything else silently returns the regular anyway.

     `--ink-muted` rather than `--ink`: the same value the poet's name takes in
     the band above, which puts the two quiet things on this page in one
     register and leaves the couplet as the only thing at full strength. */
  .bn__soon {
    font-family: var(--font-bengali);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: normal;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
